*   **Crucial Step:** Go through your AI's summary/brainstorm point by point. For each idea or statement it made, determine *where it best fits* in your new, structured blueprint document.
*   **Examples:**
    *   If the AI said, "Needs real-time stock levels," copy that to `IV.A. Inventory Core & Data Management`.
    *   If it said, "Dynamic pricing based on competitors," copy it to `IV.C. Pricing & Financials`.
    *   If it said, "AI-driven upsell recommendations," copy it to `IV.D. AI & Analytics Capabilities`.
    *   If it mentioned "Fast search for specific software licenses," that goes under `IV.E. Software Packages Specific` AND potentially `V.A. Performance & Scalability`.
    *   If it noted "Ability to track unique serial numbers for high-value items," put it in `IV.A. Inventory Core & Data Management`.
    *   If it highlighted "Reduced cost of carrying obsolete inventory," that's a direct KPI for `VI. Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)`.